Reason: each FLUDD drop remembers which player sprayed it and a mod's number for it (ext/modapi/game/modapi_world.cpp, api->water), and (split-screen co-op, ext/coop) the hit of a drop of player 2's is taken with player 2's globals in force, so an enemy it reaches is pushed away from player 2 (the game's own push reads Mario's place and facing). Alone and without mods, nothing changes.

--- a/src/Player/ModelWaterManager.cpp
